failure_location.quote:
Assume $\mu_k  \stackrel{\ast}{\rightharpoonup} \mu $ in $M(\Omega)$, then we have 
\begin{align*}
&\cE[\cN \mu_k](x) \to \cE[\cN \mu](x)  \quad \forall x \in D, \\
& \cB[\cN \mu_k](x) \to \cB[\cN \mu](x)  \quad \forall x \in \partial D.
\end{align*}

We consider the regularized Eikonal equation with homogeneous Dirichlet boundary condition
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
      |\nabla u(x)|^{2} + \epsilon \upDelta u(x) &= f^{2}(x) \quad&\forall x\in D \\
    u(x) &= 0 \quad&\forall x\in \partial D
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
